WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:15.075
and his new friends had lots of fun at Paradisle.

2
00:00:15.575 --> 00:00:20.999
They ate ice cream for breakfast, played games all afternoon, and stayed up as late as they wanted.

3
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.561
Every day really was a holiday.

4
00:00:24.622 --> 00:00:28.485
They had so much fun that they forgot how long they had been at Paradisle.

5
00:00:29.206 --> 00:00:31.508
They even forgot about their homes and families.

6
00:00:32.876 --> 00:00:35.837
For the first time, Pinocchio felt like a real boy.

7
00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:38.478
But he knew that he was still made of wood.

8
00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:42.779
So every night, he would look in the mirror, hoping to see a change.

9
00:00:43.979 --> 00:00:46.800
One night, when he looked in the mirror, he saw a change.

10
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.401
But it was not the kind of change he wanted.

11
00:00:50.161 --> 00:00:51.241
He was covered in fur!

12
00:00:52.141 --> 00:00:54.042
Just then, there was a knock at the door.

13
00:00:54.062 --> 00:00:56.963
"Pinocchio, let me in!"

14
00:00:57.583 --> 00:00:58.643
cried one of his friends.

15
00:00:59.523 --> 00:01:01.644
Pinocchio didn't want anyone to see his fur.

16
00:01:02.592 --> 00:01:04.573
"Uh, I'm not here now.

17
00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.215
Come back later," he said.

18
00:01:07.235 --> 00:01:12.577
"Pinocchio, I know you're in there because you are talking," said the boy.

19
00:01:12.597 --> 00:01:15.199
"Now let me in—hurry!"

20
00:01:16.339 --> 00:01:19.001
Pinocchio opened the door, and there stood his friend.

21
00:01:19.721 --> 00:01:20.962
He was covered in fur too!

22
00:01:20.982 --> 00:01:24.224
"Pinocchio, you have to help me!"

23
00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:25.484
the boy cried.

24
00:01:25.504 --> 00:01:27.045
"Help you?

25
00:01:27.065 --> 00:01:29.086
I don't know how to help you!

26
00:01:29.727 --> 00:01:31.888
Look at me, I'm furry too!"

27
00:01:32.456 --> 00:01:33.197
said Pinocchio.

28
00:01:34.157 --> 00:01:36.439
Both boys sat on the floor and began to cry.

29
00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:44.364
But, when they cried, they sounded like donkeys instead of boys: "Hee-haw, hee-haw!"

30
00:01:45.325 --> 00:01:47.786
Just then, there was another knock on the door.

31
00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:51.089
"Boys, are you all right in there?"

32
00:01:51.629 --> 00:01:52.870
the wagon master asked.

33
00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.131
The wagon master was their friend.

34
00:01:55.912 --> 00:01:57.293
He had brought them to Paradisle.

35
00:01:58.153 --> 00:01:59.054
He would know what to do.

36
00:01:59.074 --> 00:02:02.761
"Please, help us," they called.

37
00:02:03.821 --> 00:02:08.345
But it sounded like "Hee-haw, hee-haw."

38
00:02:10.206 --> 00:02:14.710
When the wagon master saw the boys, his smile turned to an evil laugh.

39
00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:22.876
"Ha-ha-ha! Now, it is time for you to pay for your play," he said.

40
00:02:22.896 --> 00:02:27.300
"For months, you have eaten and played without work.

41
00:02:27.992 --> 00:02:32.877
Now, you will become donkeys and work for me the rest of your lives!"

42
00:02:34.198 --> 00:02:38.081
"Donkeys?" the boys cried together.

43
00:02:38.101 --> 00:02:45.367
"But sir," said Pinocchio, "I don't want to be a donkey, I want to be a real boy."

44
00:02:46.448 --> 00:02:48.690
When the wagon master heard this, he laughed.

45
00:02:49.591 --> 00:02:50.952
"A real boy?

46
00:02:51.793 --> 00:02:54.776
All you are going to be is a real donkey."

47
00:02:55.628 --> 00:02:59.312
He quickly tied a rope around the boys' necks and led them to the ferry.

48
00:03:00.893 --> 00:03:04.536
The two boys tried to call for help, but their friends did not hear.

49
00:03:05.537 --> 00:03:07.399
They did not look like boys anymore.

50
00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.561
They looked like donkeys.

51
00:03:09.721 --> 00:03:15.967
"I will sell one of you to a farmer and the other of you to the circus.

52
00:03:16.808 --> 00:03:19.671
The circus will love a talking donkey.

53
00:03:20.311 --> 00:03:25.675
Pinocchio, I think you will make a good circus donkey since you like talking so much!"

54
00:03:27.436 --> 00:03:28.477
the man said, laughing.

55
00:03:30.818 --> 00:03:32.639
He led the two donkeys onto the ferry.

56
00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.102
There were many other sad-looking donkeys inside.

57
00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:41.165
Now, Pinocchio understood why he had seen so many donkeys that first day.

58
00:03:43.086 --> 00:03:45.548
He and all the other donkeys began to cry.
